 "_doc": "Two prints of the same account. (A) 6 bills: Munsoft-family 'TAX INVOICE / STATEMENT OF ACCOUNT' ledger (Date / Description / Reference / VAT / Debit (Inc) / Credit / Balance) with service sub-headings; electricity = basic '3ph @ > n amps' line (reference ...-BAS_ELEC_n), an energy line 'Electricity Consumption nKW - [start' (end reading truncated by the print, so only the start reading is captured) and a demand line 'Electricity Consumption nKW - [0 to n]' (max-demand register, mapped to demand_kva). (B) 5 bills: the cabedocs e-statement print whose text layer is shredded (rotated words, numbers split across columns) - they route here (VAT number present) but no electricity section is recognised, so they yield NO rows (blank over wrong); only the account is read for them, from the print-vendor tag '<!account|...'. FINGERPRINT: municipal VAT number + name/domain. total_ex_vat_r = (Debit - VAT) over the electricity lines; identity ama_check_vattotal_r = sum of electricity Debit (incl) - printed VAT TOTAL (holds because rates/interest carry no VAT; it verifies the VAT side independently, the debits only circularly). Checked on 11 bills (6 extract).",
